-- title:
--   Realising ρ' mod I in p-power torsion of J_{H_Q}
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p$ a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and $\bar\rho$ a residual Galois representation over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with an action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite subextension of $\mathbb Q$) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to $\overline k$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N\neq 0$, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra attached to $S$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit in $P$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_{\Delta,i}\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ be homomorphisms and $\alpha\in k^t$; put $L=N(\prod_i q_i)r$ and let $H_Q\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the intersection of $H_r$ with the kernel of the product of the $\pi_{\Delta,i}$. Assume the two commutativity hypotheses `OpComm` and `DiaComm` for this data (the Hecke operators on the auxiliary module commute with one another and with the diamond operators), so that the Hecke ring $\mathbb T$, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}$ of that module generated by the Hecke generators, is defined; assume $\mathbb T$ is local and $\mathcal O\to\mathbb T$ a local homomorphism. Let $\rho'$ be an adically continuous Galois representation on a free $\mathbb T$-module $V$ of rank $2$ whose trace at each Frobenius $\sigma$ at a prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ equals the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ of $\mathbb T$, and whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along $k\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathbb T$. Assume $p\nmid L$, and let $I\subseteq\mathbb T$ be an ideal with $\mathbb T/I$ finite. Then there is a homomorphism $\delta\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ which is trivial on the inertia subgroup (inside $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$) of every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit and which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite subextension of $\mathbb Q$, together with naturals $n,b$, a homomorphism $\mathrm{star}$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to the additive automorphisms of $T^b$, where $T$ is the $p^n$-torsion of $J_{H_Q}=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field of $X_{H_Q}(L)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that each component of $\mathrm{star}(\sigma)(x)$ is the image of the corresponding component of $x$ under $\sigma$ followed by the diamond operator $\langle\delta(\sigma)\rangle$, and finally a subgroup $X\subseteq T^b$ stable under $\mathrm{star}$ and a surjective additive map $\pi\colon X\to V/IV$ with $\pi(\mathrm{star}(\sigma)x)=\rho'(\sigma)\pi(x)$ for all $\sigma$ and $x\in X$, the action on $V/IV$ being the one induced by $\rho'$.
--
--   This is the realisation of the finite-level quotients $V/IV$ of the Hecke-ring-valued representation $\rho'$ inside the $p$-power torsion of the Jacobian of the modular curve $X_{H_Q}$, after twisting the geometric Galois action by a character $\delta$ that is unramified at $p$ and of finite level; in Wiles's treatment this is the passage from the cohomological construction of $\rho'$ to a geometric one. It is used by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isFlatAt_of_not_dvd_level`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isFlatAt_of_not_dvd_level), where the torsion realisation supplies the finite flat group schemes needed at $p$.
